      <div class="modal-body">
        <div class="action-seller">
          <div>The Seller will not be considered to default if the delivery does not meet the Delivery Date requirements due to delayed incoming shipments caused by logistics transportation arranged by the GigaCloud. On the specified Delivery Date, the system will set the actual warehouse receiving date to + 3 business days as the new Delivery Date. The delivery will be automatically initiated on the new Delivery Date.</div>
          <div class="desc-title">Requirements for applying for Delivery Date Protection:</div>
          <div>1. The Future Goods Contract must be associated with the Incoming Shipment (Shipping Method must be "Consigned Ocean Operation").</div>
          <div>2. Total Quantity Available must be less than the Estimated Receiving Quantity (or the sum of Estimated Receiving Quantity for multiple Incoming Shipments).</div>
          <div>3. The Delivery Date must be on or after the Marketplace''s Estimated Receiving Date of Incoming Shipment. If there are multiple Incoming Shipments, the latest Estimated Receiving Date will apply.</div>
          <div class="desc-title">Conditions when Delivery Date Protection does not apply:</div>
          <div>1. The Requested Shipping Date of the associated Incoming Shipment is modified, and the Estimated Receiving Date after modification is later than the initial Delivery Date.</div>
          <div>2. The quantity in stock after the warehouse receives the Incoming Shipment is less than the Total Quantity Available. If the quantity that can be delivered cannot meet the agreed quantity, the Seller will default to the agreement.  For multiple Future Goods Agreements, the delivery will be initiated according to the agreement fulfillment order.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="action-buyer">
          <div>The Seller has applied for the Delivery Date Protection from the GigaCloud B2B Marketplace </div>
                      <div>The Seller will not be considered to default if the delivery does not meet the Delivery Date requirements due to delayed incoming shipments caused by ocean shipping, weather, or other factors. This only applies if the following conditions are met:<br>- the Seller''s products have arrived at the originating port as requested shipping date.<br>- the Seller consigned the B2B Marketplace for ocean shipping operation.<br>If the shipment arrives after the Delivery Date, GigaCloud system will set the actual warehouse receiving date to + 3 business days as the new Delivery Date, and the delivery to Buyer will be automatically initiated on the new Delivery Date. </div>
                  </div>
      </div>
